    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Associate-Registrar--Student-Governance-and-Compliance_R31044-2": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar, Student Governance and Compliance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWho we are ?   At Torrens University Australia,   making a difference is in our DNA.   As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world.   That’s   why   we’re   on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all   walks of life   can chase their dreams.       Just like our students,   our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact . When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold,   creative   and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best.   We’ve   built a culture that celebrates community,   collaboration   and innovation, where people love what they do .       What’s the job?     The Associate Registrar   -   Student Governance and Compliance provides senior governance,   assurance   and regulatory oversight across designated Academic Services functions. The role supports the integrity of student decision-making, academic records, complaints and appeals, student safety and wellbeing processes,   completions   and related student administration.     Working across Academic Services, Student Experience, Legal, Risk,   Compliance   and academic areas, you will ensure processes are fair, consistent, evidence-based,   compliant   and auditable. You will lead or coordinate complex and high-risk matters within delegated authority, provide constructive   challenges   to operational   leaders   and advise senior stakeholders on regulatory obligations, risk,   assurance   and continuous improvement.     D ay - to - day accountabilities :   Provide governance and assurance oversight across student complaints, appeals,   misconduct   and academic integrity processes, ensuring procedural fairness and   appropriate separation   of investigation, decision-making,   review   and appeal functions.   Lead complex and high-risk matters within delegated authority,   maintaining   confidentiality, privacy, records   management   and conflict-of-interest requirements.   Coordinate the University’s responses to external complaints and investigations, including matters referred to the National Student Ombudsman, and prepare evidence-based submissions and response materials.   Oversee student wellbeing and safety processes, including escalation, reporting, referrals, incident   management   and compliance with gender-based violence prevention and response requirements.   Maintain evidence readiness, data   integrity   and audit compliance, using student voice, case   trends   and emerging risks to drive continuous improvement, particularly for students at risk and under-represented cohorts.   Establish and   maintain   a risk-based assurance framework across complaints, student safety, completions,   records   and student administration processes.   Translate legislative and regulatory requirements into clear policies, procedures, controls, evidence   requirements   and escalation pathways, including ESOS, the National Code, TEQSA, ASQA, HESF, CRICOS and PRISMS obligations.   Lead reporting on complaints, student   safety   and wellbeing, GBV, completions,   graduation   and related student administration matters, ensuring information is   accurate , privacy compliant and audit ready.   Provide oversight and assurance of completions, award eligibility, certification, graduation, student records and post-enrolment processes including progression, re-enrolment, transfers, withdrawals,   credit   and recognition of prior learning.   Provide expert advice to senior leaders and governance forums, work with Heads of Department and key stakeholders to resolve issues, and address root causes through policy review and continuous improvement.   Lead and develop a high-performing team, fostering accountability, accuracy, service, collaboration,   learning   and positive leadership.   Who you are   A postgraduate qualification in a relevant discipline, or equivalent professional experience.   Significant senior experience in academic or student administration within higher education.   Demonstrated experience managing student complaints,   appeals   and complex case resolution, including high-risk matters.   Experience leading responses to external complaints,   investigations   or regulatory bodies.   Experience overseeing student lifecycle processes, including progression, academic   records   and completions.   Advanced knowledge of the Australian higher education regulatory framework, including the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, with the ability to translate obligations into fair and auditable processes.   Strong working knowledge of the ESOS Act, National Code, TEQSA, ASQA, HESF, CRICOS and PRISMS requirements.   Experience providing leadership or assurance in student wellbeing and safety, including sensitive disclosures, incident response,   risk   and gender-based violence compliance.   Strong analytical, reporting and data governance skills, with the ability to use digital tools and AI appropriately to improve workflows, case   management   and service delivery.   Sound judgement, problem-solving, stakeholder engagement,   communication   and influencing skills, with the ability to deliver fair,   practical   and student-centred outcomes.     To read more about the role please   click here .   This is a permanent, full-time position   based   at Surry Hills Campus in Sydney.     Why join us?     Bold,   modern   and agile,   we’re   Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020,   Australian Financial Review   named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to   establish   ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people,   you’ll   find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression.      We are proud to be an   e qual opportunity employer   and   committed   to creating an inclusive workplace.   We do not discriminate   on the basis of   race, colour, religion,   age,   ethnicity,   gender identity, sexual orientation ,   disability , or any other protected characteristic.      We   encourage   applications from   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people s for all positions.       What we offer :   We support your personal passions,   development   and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At    Torrens University   Australia,   you’ll   benefit   from:       Study free in a course/degree related to your position       B Corp certified university – values   driven,   and purpose led   Access to internal opportunities - Be supported to learn,   grow   and move across the organisation           Hiring process     We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at   your career @torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring   an equitable, barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.    To learn more about   what makes Torrens University Australia   a great place   to work, visit   https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .     We’d love to hear from you.     Job   r eference:   R31044     Applications for this role will close on   Wednesday 30 th   September.     Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be   identified . You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates   regarding   your application.   If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Director-of-Employability-and-Graduate-Outcomes_R30961": {
      "title": "Director of Employability and Graduate Outcomes",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWho we are?   At   Torrens University Australia,   making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world.   That’s   why   we’re   on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all   walks of life   can chase their dreams.     Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best.   We’ve   built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do.     What’s   the job?   As the   Director of Employability and Graduate Outcomes ,   you’ll   lead the University’s strategic employability operations and drive a coordinated, institution-wide approach to improving graduate employment outcomes. Working collaboratively across Academic, Student Experience,   Growth   and Industry Engagement functions,   you’ll   align strategy, services,   partnerships   and data to support students throughout their journey   -   from career preparation and industry engagement to graduate transition.     You’ll   design,   implement   and continuously enhance the University’s employability operating model, ensuring employability is embedded throughout the student lifecycle rather than delivered as a standalone service.   You will   provide strategic input across curriculum-embedded employability, workforce and labour market intelligence and industry engagement   a s well as   driv e   student engagement with industry while leading the University’s operational employability portfolio .       You’ll   lead initiatives that strengthen student career development, expand applied learning and industry opportunities, build employer partnerships and support   graduate transition   including   during the first twelve months after completing their studies. While graduate employment outcomes are a shared institutional responsibility,   you’ll   own the operational support, governance, performance framework,   partnerships   and continuous improvement   required   to enhance these outcomes over time.     Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to):   Lead the University’s employability and graduate outcomes   operational   strategy,   governance   and performance framework.   Advise senior leaders on employability, graduate   capability   and emerging workforce trends.   Drive institution-wide improvements in graduate employment, career readiness, industry   engagement   and employer satisfaction.   Partner with   Academic leadership to   support   e mbed ding   employability, professional skills and authentic industry learning across curriculum,   assessment   and the student lifecycle.   Develop strategic partnerships with employers, industry   bodies   and professional associations to expand placements, internships, mentoring,   projects   and graduate opportunities.   Oversee careers education, employability   development   and graduate transition services, including support during the first 12 months after graduation.   Lead the operational delivery, compliance and continuous improvement of placements, applied learning and work-integrated learning.   Use graduate,   employer   and labour-market data, including QILT insights, to guide investment, measure performance and inform future workforce priorities.   Sponsor innovation, including AI-enabled employability initiatives,   new technologies   and scalable service models.   Lead and develop a high-performing employability function, managing people, budgets, resources, performance, succession   planning   and organisational capability.   Represent the University with external stakeholders and promote its position as a preferred partner for industry collaboration.   Foster a positive,   inclusive   and collaborative culture focused on accountability, innovation, professional   development   and continuous improvement.     Who you are   A senior leader with experience leading employability, workforce   development   or student success strategies in a complex organisation.   A strategic thinker and systems leader who can design and implement organisation-wide strategies and translate ambition into measurable outcomes.   An influential executive communicator who can build alignment and deliver change across multiple functions without relying solely on direct authority.   An experienced partner to academic leaders, with the ability to embed employability, professional skills and industry-connected learning within curriculum and assessment.   A relationship builder with a strong   track record   of developing employer, industry, professional   association   or sector partnerships.   Comfortable using data, performance   measures   and labour-market intelligence to inform decisions, evaluate impact and improve organisational performance.   An inclusive, coaching-oriented people leader with experience leading multidisciplinary teams, including through other people managers.   A postgraduate-qualified professional in education, business,   management   or a related discipline, or with equivalent executive experience. Qualifications in career development, organisational development, higher education, change   management   or project management will be well regarded.   Higher education experience is highly desirable, along with a strong understanding of graduate employment, future skills, curriculum   design   and employability frameworks.   To read more about the role please   click here .     This is a full-time leadership position with hybrid work flexibility. The role may be based at one of our Torrens University campuses, with occasional travel between campuses and to external forums, employer sites and industry events as   required .     Why join us?   Bold,   modern   and agile,   we’re   Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to   establish   ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people,   you’ll   find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression.     We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate   on the basis of   race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.     We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.     What we offer:   We support your personal passions,   development   and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia,   you’ll   benefit   from:   Study free in a course/degree related to your position   B Corp certified university – values driven, and purpose led   Access to internal opportunities - Be supported to learn,   grow   and move across the organisation   Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.     If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact   us   at   yourcareer @torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring   an equitable , barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.     To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia   a great place   to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog.   We’d   love to hear from you.     Job reference: R30961     Applications for this role will close on   Fr iday   1 8 th   September.   Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be  identified . You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates  regarding  your application.   If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Flinders/Student-Services-Advisor--Campus-_R30932": {
      "title": "Student Services Advisor (Campus)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nStudent Services Advisor   Student Experience | Customer Service | Higher Education   About the Opportunit y   Are you a student-focused customer service professional who enjoys solving problems and helping people navigate important moments in their education?   As a Student Services Advisor,   you'll   play a key role in   delivering   a consistent , high-quality campus experience for new and existing students .   You'll   take ownership of enquiries from start to finish, working with teams across Torrens University to provide clear information, resolve   issues   and help students progress confidently through their studies.   This is an exciting opportunity for someone who enjoys being visible and accessible on campus, thrives in a fast-paced, target-led environment, and takes pride in turning complex questions into positive student experiences.   If   you're   passionate about student success and delivering service with empathy,   accuracy   and accountability,   we'd   love to hear from you.   What's   in it for you   Full-time opportunity based at our Flinders Campus on a 12-month fixed-term contract.   Make a visible, meaningful difference to students on campus every day   Work collaboratively with academic, professional and student support teams   Access professional development and career growth opportunities   Be part of a collaborative, inclusive and continuously improving culture     What You'll Do   You'll   provide responsive, end-to-end support that helps students access the information,   services   and solutions they need to succeed.     Responsibilities include:   Act as a welcoming first point of contact for students attending campus with questions or concerns   Manage student enquiries from beginning to end, meeting service standards and agreed   timeframes   Resolve enquiries relating to system access, subject   selection , enrolment, timetables, student   finance   and progression   Provide   accurate   support for admissions, transcripts, statements of attainment and academic administration processes   Support international students with enrolment compliance and visa or Confirmation of Enrolment enquiries, within role boundaries   Work closely with Faculty, Learning Services, Technology Support, Student Records, Academic Administration and Student Finance teams   Escalate complex matters appropriately while   remaining   a consistent point of contact until resolution   Assist   students to resolve informal complaints and contribute to improved satisfaction,   effort   and advocacy scores   Identify   opportunities to use student feedback and voice-of-customer insights to improve processes and service delivery   Participate in team meetings, orientation, information   sessions   and campus events as   required     Skills & Experience     Must Have   At least two years' experience in a front-of-house, customer   service   or customer experience role   A proven commitment to delivering high-quality, student- centred   or customer-focused service   Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain information clearly   Strong analytical,   problem-solving   and decision-making skills   The ability to build effective relationships across teams and work collaboratively to achieve outcomes   The ability to   organise ,   prioritise   and work autonomously in a target- and KPI-driven environment     Nice to Have   Experience working in higher education, vocational   education   or a similarly regulated service environment   Working knowledge of Salesforce, Microsoft   Dynamics   or comparable case-management systems   Understanding of student administration, academic   processes   or international student compliance requirements   Why Join Torrens?   At Torrens University Australia,   we're   transforming lives through education. As a Certified B Corporation,   we're   committed to making a positive impact by providing industry-relevant education that helps students build meaningful careers.   Our people are driven by purpose,   collaboration   and innovation.   You'll   join a diverse community that values accessibility, empathy, resolution,   personalisation ,   speed   and choice in every student interaction.   Together,   we're   creating exceptional learning experiences and a supportive environment where students,   colleagues   and communities can thrive.   How to Apply   Click APPLY to   submit   your application.   Applications close:   24th September 2026   Once you apply, we'll keep you updated throughout the recruitment process.   Hiring Process   Application review   Interview(s)   Reference and background checks   Offer   Should you have accessibility requirements or needs, please contact   Sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au   for confidential support to ensure   an equitable , barrier-free application process.   About Torrens University Australia   Torrens University Australia is a young, global university committed to transforming lives through education.   We offer industry-relevant programs designed to prepare students for meaningful careers in a rapidly changing world.   We foster a collaborative, inclusive and purpose-led culture where innovation, professional growth and continuous improvement are valued. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
