rovide   accurate   support for admissions, transcripts, statements of attainment and academic administration processes   Support international students with enrolment compliance and visa or Confirmation of Enrolment enquiries, within role boundaries   Work closely with Faculty, Learning Services, Technology Support, Student Records, Academic Administration and Student Finance teams   Escalate complex matters appropriately while   remaining   a consistent point of contact until resolution   Assist   students to resolve informal complaints and contribute to improved satisfaction,   effort   and advocacy scores   Identify   opportunities to use student feedback and voice-of-customer insights to improve processes and service delivery   Participate in team meetings, orientation, information   sessions   and campus events as   required   Skills & Experience   Must Have   At least two years' experience in a front-of-house, customer   service   or customer experience role   A proven commitment to delivering high-quality, student- centred   or customer-focused service   Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain information clearly   Strong analytical,   problem-solving   and decision-making skills   The ability to build effective relationships across teams and work collaboratively to achieve outcomes   The ability to   organise ,   prioritise   and work autonomously in a target- and KPI-driven environment     Nice to Have   Experience working in higher education, vocational   education   or a similarly regulated service environment   Working knowledge of Salesforce, Microsoft   Dynamics   or comparable case-management systems   Understanding of student administration, academic   processes   or international student compliance requirements     Why Join Torrens?   At Torrens University Australia,   we're   transforming lives through education. As a Certified B Corporation,   we're   committed to making a positive impact by providing industry-relevant education that helps students build meaningful careers.   Our people are driven by purpose,   collaboration   and innovation.   You'll   join a diverse community that values accessibility, empathy, resolution,   personalisation ,   speed   and choice in every student interaction.   Together,   we're   creating exceptional learning experiences and a supportive environment where students,   colleagues   and communities can thrive.   How to Appl y   Click APPLY to   submit   your application.   Applications close: 24th September 2026 Once you apply, we'll keep you updated throughout the recruitment process.   Hiring Process   Application review   Interview(s)   Reference and background checks   Offer   Should you have accessibility requirements or needs, please contact   Sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au   for confidential support to ensure   an equitable , barrier-free application process.   About Torrens University Australia   Torrens University Australia is a young, global university committed to transforming lives through education.   We offer industry-relevant programs designed to prepare students for meaningful careers in a rapidly changing world.   We foster a collaborative, inclusive and purpose-led culture where innovation, professional growth and continuous improvement are valued.   If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
