    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Brisbane/Student-Services-Team-Leader--Campus-_R30906": {
      "title": "Student Services Team Leader (Campus)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nStudent Services Team Leader   Student Services | Campus Experience | Student Support     About   the Opportunity   Are you an experienced student services leader who is passionate about delivering exceptional, student- centred   support?   As a Student Services Team Leader,   you'll   lead a team of Student Services Advisors at our Brisbane campus, providing high-quality support to new and existing students through face-to-face interactions and online platforms. Reporting to the Student Services Manager (Campus),   you'll   oversee day-to-day service delivery, meet agreed service   levels   and help ensure students receive   a consistent , best-in-class experience.   This is a student-facing, campus-based role for a people-focused leader who can balance coaching and development with   accurate ,   timely   and target-driven service delivery. You will work closely with Campus Operations and teams across the University to resolve complex enquiries, improve   processes   and support a respectful, high-performing culture.   If   you're   a calm,   organised   and collaborative leader who enjoys making a visible difference to students,   we'd   love to hear from you.   What's   in it for you   12-month fixed-term, full-time opportunity based at our Brisbane campus   Lead and develop a team that makes a direct impact on the student experience   Work across Student Services, Campus Operations, academic   teams   and specialist support areas   Join Australia's largest private university and a purpose-led   organisation     What You'll Do   You'll lead the campus-based Student Services team while supporting a positive,   responsive   and student- centred   experience for everyone who studies at Torrens University   Australia.     Responsibilities include:   Supervise Student Services Advisors (Campus) and oversee customer service processes in line with TGE procedures,   policies   and service line agreements.   Meet KPIs and service levels for customer experience and satisfaction, ensuring student enquiries are handled accurately and within agreed   timeframes .   Support the team with student enquiries when   required , resolve complex   issues   and escalate matters appropriately.   Coordinate large-scale administrative tasks and contribute to continuous improvement activities that support   accurate , compliant student records and service delivery.   Support the Student Services Manager (Campus) to roll out new processes and   procedures, and   actively   identify   opportunities to improve   the student   experience.   Provide international student administration support, including   enrolment   compliance and visa/ CoE   enquiries, in line with external regulatory requirements and company policies. Staff must not provide   visa   or migration advice.   Provide   accurate   information for tuition   fee   and invoice enquiries, including processing payments of tuition fees and incidental fees.   Analyse   student feedback across relevant channels to   identify   service enhancements and positively influence Net Promoter Score, Student Effort   Score   and Student Satisfaction Score.   Maintain strong stakeholder relationships and   participate   in team meetings, events,   Orientation   and Information Sessions as   required .     Leadership responsibilities include:   Lead,   direct   and develop a high-performing team focused on accountability, efficiency,   accuracy   and service to students.   Support recruitment, workforce planning, succession planning, capability   development   and resource risk management.   Drive engagement through regular communication, coaching, team meetings, 1:1s, professional development support and action planning.   Complete performance management activities when   required , including goal setting,   monitoring   and formal feedback conversations.   Build collaborative relationships across the University, model positive leadership and actively support company initiatives.     Skills & Experience   Must Have   Bachelor   degree in a related field (Business/Commerce) is preferred.   5+ years of experience in administrative support roles, preferably in a higher education environment.   Prior leadership or management experience, with a demonstrated ability to coach and develop a team.   Working knowledge of the Higher Education Support Act, ESOS Act (2000), National Code 2018 and PRISMS and/or tertiary education student records systems is preferred.   Proficiency   in Excel and the ability to work confidently across multiple systems and platforms.   Strong student or customer service and engagement skills, with excellent written and verbal communication.   Excellent self-directed time management,   organisation   and   prioritisation   skills, with the ability to meet strict deadlines in a fast-paced environment.   The ability to work autonomously, take initiative, follow policies and procedures, and   identify   when to escalate an issue or seek support.   A proactive, reliable approach, strong attention to detail,   honesty   and   a high level   of integrity.   Availability to work in line with campus operating hours, including occasional out-of-hours or weekend work when   required .     How to Apply   Click APPLY to   submit   your application.   Applications   close:   18 th   September 2026   Once you apply, we'll keep you updated throughout the recruitment process.   Hiring Process   Application Review   Interview(s)   Reference & Background Checks   Offer     Should you have accessibility requirements or needs, please contact sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support to ensure   an equitable , barrier-free application process.   About Torrens University Australia   At Torrens University Australia,   we're   transforming lives through education. As a Certified B Corporation,   we're   committed to making a positive impact by providing industry-relevant education that helps students build meaningful careers.   Our Student Services team plays   an important role   in creating accessible,   responsive   and supportive experiences that help students connect,   participate   and thrive throughout their studies.   Our Culture   Our people are passionate about innovation,   collaboration   and creating exceptional student experiences.   We foster an inclusive, high-performing environment where ideas are valued, initiative is   encouraged   and professional growth is supported.   You'll   work with colleagues across the University who are committed to making a positive difference for students and the communities we serve.   If   you're   looking to build your career while helping students succeed,   we'd   love to hear from you. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Campus-Life-Coordinator_R30696": {
      "title": "Campus Life Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCampus Life Coordinator   Student Experience | Campus Engagement | Health, Safety & Wellbeing   About the Opportunity   Are you a people-focused professional who enjoys creating welcoming,   connected   and engaging campus experiences?   As a Campus Life Coordinator,   you'll   be a visible and approachable presence at our Surry Hills campus, helping students and staff get the most from their campus experience. Reporting to the Campus Director,   you'll   deliver campus activities, support student   engagement   and help ensure the campus is accessible,   collaborative   and welcoming. This is a hands-on opportunity for someone who enjoys turning ideas into action   -   from setting up spaces and supporting events to coordinating communications,   Orientation   and student activities.   You'll   also play   an important role   in monitoring campus WHS matters and   coordinating   the Campus WHS Committee, including volunteer First Aiders,   Wardens   and Mental Health First Aiders.   If   you're   proactive,   resourceful   and passionate about creating exceptional student experiences,   we'd   love to hear from you.   What's   in it for you   Permanent full-time opportunity based at our Surry Hills campus   Make a visible difference to student life and campus culture   Work closely with students, staff, academic   teams   and campus partners   Join Australia's largest private university and a purpose-led   organisation     What You'll Do   You'll help bring our campus activation strategy to life while supporting a positive, student- centred   experience for everyone who studies,   works   and visits at Surry Hills.   Responsibilities include:   Coordinate campus activities for students, industry and staff, including events, campus tours, student   activities   and Information Sessions.   Be a visible and engaged point of contact on campus, providing support to students and staff and helping resolve issues where needed.   Coordinate Orientation activities, including hosting the International Student Welcome session and supporting international students through drop-in sessions and guidance.   Work with Campus Directors, Program Directors and accommodation providers to support the welfare,   attendance   and academic progress of international students under 18, in line with ESOS requirements and relevant procedures.   Work closely with the SRC, supporting student-led   initiatives   and   providing   practical guidance.   Coordinate staff and student communications on campus, including newsletters, signage,   notices   and digital displays.   Monitor WHS matters across campus, support workplace inspections,   maintain   risk   information   and help raise awareness of health,   safety   and security requirements.   Lead and   coordinate   the Campus WHS Committee, including volunteer First Aiders,   Wardens   and Mental Health First Aiders.   Support the Property and Facilities team and National HSS Manager with safety and security initiatives, including relevant systems,   procedures   and campus awareness activities.     Skills & Experience   Must Have   Experience in   a front -of-house, customer service, hospitality or customer experience role; experience in a campus or higher education environment is advantageous.   A genuine passion for helping people and creating a welcoming,   accessible   and student- centred   experience.   A visible, hands-on approach and the confidence to get involved in setting up spaces, supporting   events   and delivering initiatives.   Strong relationship-building and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with students, staff, academic   teams   and external partners.   The ability to work autonomously, take ownership and use initiative while also following direction and established procedures.   Demonstrated ability to schedule and   prioritise   effectively, manage competing   priorities   and remain responsive in a fast-paced environment.   Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with strong administration and attention to detail.   Availability to work in line with campus operating hours, including occasional out-of-hours or weekend work when   required .   Nice to Have   Knowledge or experience in workplace health and safety, risk   management   or campus safety processes.   Current First Aid certification, or a willingness to obtain it.   Experience coordinating volunteers, committees,   events   or student engagement initiatives.   Working knowledge of Microsoft Dynamics or another CRM/customer management platform.     How to Apply   Click APPLY to   submit   your application.   Applications   close:   18 th   September 2026   Once you apply, we'll keep you updated throughout the recruitment process.   Hiring Process   Application Review   Interview(s)   Reference & Background Checks   Offer     Should you have accessibility requirements or needs, please contact sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au for confidential support to ensure   an equitable , barrier-free application process.   About Torrens University Australia   At Torrens University Australia,   we're   transforming lives through education. As a Certified B Corporation,   we're   committed to making a positive impact by providing industry-relevant education that helps students build meaningful careers.   Our Campus Experience team plays   an important role   in creating engaging,   accessible   and collaborative learning spaces where students can connect,   participate   and thrive.   Our Culture   Our people are passionate about innovation, collaboration and creating exceptional student experiences.   We foster an inclusive, high-performing environment where ideas are valued, initiative is   encouraged   and professional growth is supported.   You'll   work with colleagues across the University who are committed to making a positive difference for students and the communities we serve.   If   you're   looking to build your career while helping create a campus experience that makes a real impact,   we'd   love to hear from you.   If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
