    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Flinders/Academic-Administration-Coordinator_R31104-1": {
      "title": "Academic Administration Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWho we are?   At   Torrens University Australia,   making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world.   That’s   why   we’re   on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all   walks of life   can chase their dreams.     Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best.   We’ve   built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do.   What’s   the job?   As the   Academic Administration Coordinator ,   you’ll   provide customer-focused academic support and course administration across the student lifecycle.   You’ll   work with academic leaders, faculty   members   and University stakeholders to support academic governance, course administration, student results processing, records   management   and project delivery.   You’ll   help ensure academic administration processes are   accurate ,   compliant   and focused on student success.   You’ll   coordinate governance requirements,   maintain   the integrity of course and student data, support course   accreditation   and review activities, and contribute to process improvements that strengthen academic quality and service delivery.   Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to):   Implement faculty-wide academic administration process improvements across the student lifecycle.   Coordinate the administration of academic governance committees, including Learning and Teaching, Examination, Academic Progression, Curriculum and Course Advisory committees.   Maintain   accurate   and reliable   course , subject and student data across academic administration systems and processes.   Support compliance with relevant legislation, regulatory standards, professional   requirements,   and University policies.   Support course accreditation, course review, material change   notifications   and professional association submissions.   Develop and implement teach-out and transition plans, ensuring appropriate administrative coordination.   Coordinate course and subject review processes, including data validation,   reporting,   and stakeholder updates.   Ensure student results are processed and distributed accurately and on time, in line with policy and the academic calendar.   Maintain the integrity of student records, academic transcripts, parchments, graduation   documentation,   and certification records.   Manage antecedent institution and archived records, respond to student records enquiries, and undertake privacy and data integrity checks.   Track project timelines,   deliverables   and risks, providing clear status   updates,   and coordinating follow-up actions.   Contribute to internal audits, risk management, continuous   improvement,   and the development of high-performing academic administration practices.   Who you are   An experienced academic administration professional with at least three years’ experience in higher education,   VET   or a dual-sector environment.   A bachelor’s degree or relevant equivalent experience, with qualifications in project, process or change management highly regarded.   Knowledge of TEQSA, ASQA, the Higher Education Standards Framework, Standards for RTOs 2015, ESOS and the National Code 2018.   Experience in student records, results processing, certification documentation, academic   governance   or course administration.   Demonstrated ability to manage projects and deliver measurable process and service improvements, using Lean, Six   Sigma   or similar approaches.   Highly organised and detail-focused, with strong data management, reporting and problem-solving skills and the ability to manage competing priorities.   A collaborative and confident communicator who can build productive relationships with academic leaders, professional   teams   and other stakeholders.   A student-focused, solutions-oriented professional who values quality, compliance, accuracy,   teamwork   and continuous improvement.     To read more about the role please   click here .   This is a full-time permanent role based at any of our four campuses.   Why join us?   Bold,   modern   and agile,   we’re   Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2,000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to   establish   ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people,   you’ll   find opportunities for professional development and career progression.   We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate   on the basis of   race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.   We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.   What we offer:   We support your personal passions,   development   and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia,   you’ll   benefit   from:   Study free in a course or degree related to your position   Access to internal opportunities – be supported to learn,   grow   and move across the organisation   A values-driven and purpose-led working environment   Hiring process :   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.   If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact us at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring   an equitable , barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.   To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia   a great place   to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog.   We’d   love to hear from you.   Job reference:   R31104      Applications for this role will close on   Friday 9 th  October .   Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be   identified . You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates   regarding   your application.   If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Wakefield/Learning-Facilitator_R31016-1": {
      "title": "Learning Facilitator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLearning Facilitator   Health Science | Academic | Adelaide   About the Opportunity   Are you a passionate health science educator who enjoys helping students build the knowledge,   skills   and confidence they need for successful careers?   As a Learning Facilitator,   you’ll   prepare,   deliver   and assess subjects across a range of learning environments, including on campus and online.   You’ll   work with academic colleagues and program leaders to create engaging learning experiences, support student   progress   and ensure assessment and academic processes are delivered to a high standard.   This is an opportunity to contribute to a student- centred   academic environment through innovative teaching,   timely   feedback, course   review   and quality improvement. Depending on program needs and your   expertise , you may also contribute to subject or program coordination, specialist academic projects, industry engagement, research, mentoring or other academic leadership activities.   If   you’re   committed to high-quality teaching and want to make a meaningful difference in the education of future health professionals,   we’d   love to hear from you.   What's   in it for you   Join a student-focused academic team based at our Adelaide campus   Teach and support learners across on-campus and online environments   Contribute to contemporary health science education and course improvement   Access professional development, academic   collaboration   and career growth opportunities   Make a meaningful impact on student learning,   progression   and success     What You'll Do   You’ll create inclusive, engaging learning experiences and help students achieve their learning outcomes throughout the study period.   Responsibilities include:   Deliver lectures, seminars, forums, workshops, practical sessions and tutorials using innovative teaching and learning practices   Prepare, review and update subject materials in response to program requirements and quality measures   Develop, review, set and mark assessments and examination papers as   required   Assess student work and provide   timely , constructive feedback that supports learning and improvement   Apply academic policies and processes,   determine   final results   and   submit   outcomes by required deadlines   Participate in validation, moderation, course   review   and assessment review activities   Identify students who may be at risk and make   appropriate referrals   to academic, language,   wellbeing   and student-success support services   Monitor and record student attendance and participation as   required   Understand how   allocated   subjects fit within the broader course architecture and contribute to continuous improvement   Contribute to agreed academic, professional practice, research, mentoring,   coordination   or specialist project responsibilities     Skills & Experience   Must Have   Relevant qualifications and/or professional   expertise   in Health Science or a related discipline   Experience teaching or   facilitating   learning in higher education, vocational   education   or a relevant professional setting   Demonstrated ability to prepare and deliver engaging learning activities across face-to-face and online environments   Experience designing,   marking   or reviewing assessments and providing high-quality student feedback   Strong understanding of academic integrity, assessment processes,   moderation   and quality assurance   Excellent communication,   organisation   and interpersonal skills, with a student- centred   approach   Ability to   identify   student support needs, make   appropriate referrals   and work collaboratively with academic and professional teams     Nice to Have   Experience in subject or program coordination, course   review   or academic quality improvement   Industry or professional practice engagement relevant to Health Science   Experience mentoring academic staff or leading specialist academic projects   Research experience or an interest in contributing to scholarship and research activities     For more information, please   click here .     Why Join Torrens?   Join an institution committed to transforming education through innovation,   technology   and exceptional student experiences.   You'll   help shape the future of higher education while working alongside passionate professionals dedicated to student success,   organisational   excellence   and meaningful outcomes.   We foster a collaborative, inclusive and purpose-led culture where innovation, professional growth and continuous improvement are valued.   You'll   join a team that embraces   new ideas , supports one   another   and is committed to delivering meaningful impact for students,   colleagues   and the broader community.   How to Apply   Click   APPLY   to   submit   your application.   Applications close:   8 th  October 2026   Once you apply, we'll keep you updated throughout the recruitment process.   Hiring Process   Application Review    Interview(s)    Reference & Background Checks    Offer      Should you have accessibility requirements or needs, please contact   Sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au   for confidential support to ensure   an equitable , barrier-free application process.   About Torrens University Australia   At Torrens University Australia,   we're   transforming lives through education. As a Certified B Corporation,   we're   committed to making a positive impact by providing industry-relevant education that helps students build meaningful careers.   Our people are driven by purpose,   collaboration   and innovation. Together,   we're   creating exceptional learning experiences that prepare students for success in a rapidly changing world. If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Wakefield/Learning-Facilitator_R31037": {
      "title": "Learning Facilitator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLearning Facilitator Bachelor of Nursing | Wakefield Campus | Full-time   Who we are:   At Torrens University Australia , making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams. Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration and innovation, where people love what they do. The Opportunity As part of our Bachelor of Nursing program , we are proud to educate students and enable them to become great nurses. We know you are a passionate educator with current nursing registration seeking a role where you can make a positive difference in the present and future of nursing education. This role is a terrific opportunity to combine your motivation and energy and join our collaborative team based at our Wakefield Campus. You will work to ensure students are provided with the best opportunity to attain learning outcomes. There will also be opportunity to keep up to on your discipline by undertaking professional development activities to further your knowledge and skills to help create the nurses of tomorrow. This is a permanent full-time position based at our Wakefield Campus. Courses are taught over the course of 3 trimesters per year, each trimester consisting of 12-week blocks. Reporting to the Course Coordinator, you will be responsible for:   Delivery and teaching of the Nursing Program content utilising flexible learning modes to accommodate student needs ensuring compliance with all regulatory frameworks Mentor students to understand and utilise the Codes and Standards of Professional Practice relating to Nursing Utilise learning technology effectively and embed in design and delivery Engage in student centred learning and teaching practices and maintaining an active and positive education experience Engage in a model best practice in applying pedagogical principles, instructional strategies, and communication strategies appropriate to the learners. Provide on-going assessment support for students to satisfactorily complete assessment tasks    Who are you ? To be successful in the Bachelor of Nursing – Learning Facilitator position you MUST have (TEQSA requirement):      Experience in education/training and assessment    Understanding of pedagogical and/or adult learning principles relevant to the student cohort being taught.    Masters qualification in nursing   Current Division 1 Nurse Registration with AHPRA   Sound understanding of current scholarship and/or professional practice in the discipline that is being taught    To read more about the role please click here to view job description Why join us? Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.   Hiring process    We aim to provide you with the necessary information you need at each stage of this process to put your best self forward. If you want to know more, or need assistance or accommodation during the recruiting phase, please contact your recruiter at sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog.   We’d love to hear from you.  Applications close: 6th October 2026 JR: R31037 If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Ellucian-Banner-Tech-Lead_R30616-1": {
      "title": "Ellucian Banner Tech Lead",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWho we are ?   At Torrens University Australia,   making a difference is in our DNA.   As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world.   That’s   why   we’re   on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all   walks of life   can chase their dreams.       Just like our students,   our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact . When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold,   creative   and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best.   We’ve   built a culture that celebrates community,   collaboration   and innovation, where people love what they do .       What’s the job?   The Ellucian Banner Tech Lead  is responsible for  leading the design, development, and delivery of Ellucian Banner ERP solutions across the organisation. This role combines hands on technical  expertise  with cloud service models, including Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS) and Software-as-a-Service (SaaS), and the integration with enterprise education systems such as Ellucian Banner.       Operating within Torrens University landscape, the role will drive Banner solution architecture and guide development practices across Banner and integrated platforms, including Salesforce CRM systems, learning management systems (Canvas), and middleware technologies such as Informatica.       Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to):     Provide technical leadership and governance for the Ellucian Banner ecosystem,   establishing   and enforcing development standards, coding practices, architectural principles, and quality assurance processes across Banner applications, Oracle databases, integrations, and supporting technologies.   Lead the design, development, enhancement, and support of Banner ERP solutions across Student, Finance, Human Resources, Payroll, and related modules, ensuring solutions align with institutional   objectives , regulatory requirements, and business processes.   Act as the senior technical authority for Banner architecture, designing scalable and sustainable solutions that align with enterprise architecture standards and support integration with platforms including CRM, LMS, identity management, reporting, data warehouse, and middleware solutions.   Design, develop, and oversee Banner integrations using Banner APIs, Ethos Integration, Application Navigator, Oracle PL/SQL, web services, ETL frameworks, and middleware platforms, ensuring secure, reliable, and high-quality data exchange across enterprise systems.   Provide advanced technical   expertise   in Oracle database administration, Banner customisation, performance tuning, troubleshooting, and root cause analysis, serving as the highest escalation point for complex production issues and critical incidents.     Who you are    8+ years of experience supporting, developing, and administering Ellucian Banner ERP within a higher education environment.   Demonstrated experience in a Banner Technical Lead, Senior Banner Developer, Solutions Architect, or equivalent technical leadership role.   Extensive experience with Banner architecture, Oracle databases, SQL, PL/SQL, Banner Extensibility, Application Navigator, and Job Submission processes.   Proven experience designing, developing, and supporting Banner integrations using Ethos, Integration Hub, APIs, web services, middleware platforms, and enterprise integration patterns.   Experience delivering integrations between Banner and enterprise applications including LMS, CRM, identity management, finance, HR, reporting, and data warehouse platforms     To read more about the role please   click here .     This is a   full-time permanent role with   h ybrid flexibility and is based at our Surry Hills Campus in Sydney. Candidates must have full, ongoing working rights in Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.   Why join us?      Bold,  modern  and agile,  we’re  Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020,  Australian Financial Review  named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to  establish  ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people,  you’ll  find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression.      We are proud to be an   e qual opportunity employer   and   committed   to creating an inclusive workplace.   We do not discriminate   on the basis of   race, colour, religion,   age,   ethnicity,   gender identity, sexual orientation ,   disability , or any other protected characteristic.      We   encourage   applications from   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people s for all positions.       What we offer :   We support your personal passions,   development   and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At  Torrens University   Australia,   you’ll   benefit   from:       Study free in a course/degree related to your position       B Corp certified university – values   driven,   and purpose led   Access to internal opportunities - Be supported to learn,   grow   and move across the organisation           Hiring process: We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au   for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring   an equitable , barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.     To learn more about   what makes Torrens University Australia   a great place   to work, visit   https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .     We’d love to hear from you.     Job   r eference:   R30616     To ensure a fair and thorough review process, applications for this role will close on  Thursday 1st October. You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates  regarding  your application.  Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be identified.     If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Student-Complaints-Officer_R31112": {
      "title": "Student Complaints Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nWho we are?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.     Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact. When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative, and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration, and innovation, where people love what they do.     What’s the job?   As the Student Complaints Officer , you’ll support the Student Complaints Manager to manage and resolve a significant volume of student complaints and appeals, including matters relating to academic integrity and generative AI. You’ll help ensure each matter is handled fairly, consistently and transparently, while keeping students informed and maintaining accurate , auditable records.     You’ll investigate complaints and appeals, assess evidence, prepare clear case summaries and recommendations, and draft outcome correspondence in plain English. You’ll provide practical advice on the Student Complaints Policy and related procedures, work with academic and professional teams on complex matters, and contribute to improvements that strengthen confidence in the University’s complaint-handling processes.     Principal accountabilities include (but are not limited to):   Triage new appeals, set priorities and maintain momentum across a high-volume caseload.   Gather and test evidence, liaise with relevant parties, verify policy application and assess appropriate remedies .   Prepare accurate reports, succinct case summaries, recommendations and plain-English outcome letters.   Keep complainants and appellants informed about processes, timelines and outcomes, de-escalating concerns where possible.   Identify and refer urgent welfare or safety risks through established pathways.   Apply policies and procedures consistently, ensuring procedural fairness, independence and the absence of conflicts of interest.   Meet acknowledgement and resolution timeframes , recording defensible reasons for any extensions.   Safeguard privacy and confidentiality and maintain accurate records in approved records management systems.   Provide specialist advice on appeals, including academic integrity breaches and generative AI use.   Work with the Student Complaints Manager, Policy and Academic Governance, Legal and relevant offices on complex or high-risk matters.   Contribute to complaint-handling resources, training, benchmarking and continuous improvement activities.   Build respectful relationships with students, academics and professional staff while delivering outstanding service.     Who you are :   An experienced complaints or case management professional with at least five years’ experience managing student complaints, preferably within a university or comparable education environment.   Confident handling appeals and complaints involving academic integrity issues, including the use of generative AI.   Highly organised and detail-focused, with the ability to manage a high-volume workload accurately and efficiently.   A clear and empathetic communicator who can write concise, well-reasoned correspondence for diverse audiences, including people who speak English as an additional language.   Knowledgeable in administrative policies, procedures, privacy, procedural fairness and records management.   Collaborative and resilient, with a student-service mentality and the judgement to balance people, compliance and organisational needs.   Technically capable, including strong skills in word processing, spreadsheets and enterprise records management systems.   An undergraduate-qualified professional, or someone with equivalent relevant experience.     To read more about the role please click here .   This is a full-time permanent role based at our Surry Hills  campus in Sydney . Offering hybrid flexibility to work from home or allocated campus days .     Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2,000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find opportunities for professional development and career progression.     We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.     We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all positions.     What we offer:   We support your personal passions, development and wellbeing, to make your working life a more rewarding experience. At Torrens University Australia, you’ll benefit from:   Study free in a course or degree related to your position   Access to internal opportunities – be supported to learn, grow and move across the organisation   A values-driven and purpose-led working environment   Hiring process :   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self.     If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact us at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable , barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.     To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog.   We’d love to hear from you.     Job reference: R31112     Applications for this role will close on Wednesday 14 October.     Please note, we may close applications earlier should a suitable candidate be identified . You can expect to hear from our Talent Acquisition team after this date with updates regarding your application.   If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Student-Communications-Officer_R31101": {
      "title": "Student Communications Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nStudent Communications Officer   Student Experience | Communications | Student Engagement   | 76K + Super About the Opportunity   Are you a clear and creative communicator who enjoys making complex information easy to understand and helping students stay informed and engaged?   As a Student Communications Officer,   you'll   develop and coordinate   timely ,   accurate   and engaging communications across the student journey. Working across email, SMS, the Student Hub, student   publications   and other digital platforms,   you'll   turn academic, administrative, policy and operational information into accessible, student-friendly content.   You'll   work closely with academic, operational,   marketing   and student support teams to coordinate communications,   maintain   content schedules, support   governance   and improve engagement through student feedback and communication data.   This is a permanent, full-time position that can be based   at   any of our four campuses.   If   you're   passionate about thoughtful, inclusive communications and creating a better student experience,   we'd   love to hear from you.   What's   in it for you   •   Make a direct contribution to a clear, connected and student- centred   experience   •   Work across varied communication channels,   campaigns   and student lifecycle priorities   •   Collaborate with academic, operational, marketing and student support teams   •   Contribute to a diverse and inclusive education environment with opportunities to grow   What You'll Do   You'll   create and coordinate communications that inform,   support   and engage students across Torrens   University Australia .   You'll   bring structure to communication planning and help ensure messages are   accurate , accessible, well   timed   and aligned with   organisational   priorities.   Responsibilities include:   •   Develop,   edit   and deliver clear,   accurate   and engaging student communications across email, SMS, the Student Hub, digital   publications   and other platforms.   •   Coordinate communications covering enrolment, orientation, progression, census, assessment, wellbeing, student support,   events   and important service updates.   •   Translate complex information into clear and inclusive content tailored to different student cohorts and stages of the student journey.   •   Maintain the student communications calendar, manage content   schedules   and help resolve message overlaps and high-volume communication periods.   •   Develop communication plans for significant student activities, initiatives and events, and support regular publications and campaigns.   •   Apply content governance, approval and quality assurance processes, and use engagement data and feedback to   identify   improvements.   Skills & Experience   Must Have   •   A post-secondary qualification in communications, media, journalism, marketing or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience,   education   and training.   •   Demonstrated experience developing,   editing   and proofreading effective written communications for diverse audiences across multiple channels.   •   Strong writing skills and the ability to translate complex information into concise, engaging and student-friendly content.   •   Strong stakeholder,   organisational   and project coordination skills, with sound judgement, attention to detail and the ability to manage competing deadlines.   •   Knowledge of digital accessibility, plain   English   and inclusive communication principles.   Nice to Have   •   Experience working in higher education, vocational   education   or another regulated service environment.   •   Experience managing content in a Student Hub, student portal,   intranet   or content management system, including Sitecore or a similar platform.   •   Experience using customer relationship management, email   marketing   or student communication platforms, and developing communications for international and culturally diverse audiences.   How to Apply   Click APPLY to   submit   your application.   Applications close: 11 October Once you apply, we'll keep you updated throughout the recruitment process.   Hiring Process   •   Application Review   •   Interview(s)   •   Reference & Background Checks   •   Offer   Should you have accessibility requirements or needs, please contact the recruiter at   sebastian.pabon@torrens.edu.au   for confidential support to ensure   an equitable , barrier-free application process.   About Torrens   University Australia   We are committed to delivering accessible, industry-relevant education and creating student experiences that support learners to succeed.   Our teams work across a diverse student community, collaborating to provide clear information, practical   support   and connected experiences throughout the student journey.   Our Culture   Our people are passionate about innovation, collaboration and creating exceptional student experiences.   We foster an inclusive, high-performing environment where ideas are valued, professional growth is   supported   and people are encouraged to make a meaningful contribution.   You'll   work alongside committed colleagues who care about students and the quality of their experience.   If   you're   looking to develop your communications career while contributing to a purpose-led education   organisation ,   we'd   love to hear from you.   If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    },
    "https://strayer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ANZ_TUA_External1/job/Campus-Surry-Hills/Financial-Accountant_R31154-1": {
      "title": "Financial Accountant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWho we are ?   At Torrens University Australia, making a difference is in our DNA. As a Certified B Corporation, we belong to a global community of future-focused companies using business as a force for good. We believe in the transformative power of education to change lives, families, communities – and the world. That’s why we’re on a mission to increase access to higher education, so learners from all walks of life can chase their dreams.     Just like our students, our employees are a diverse group who want to make an impact . When you join us, we give you the freedom to be bold, creative and courageous – with flexible working arrangements that allow you to bring your best. We’ve built a culture that celebrates community, collaboration and innovation, where people love what they do .     What’s the job?     Preparing month end journals and reconciliations across various areas which may include cash , intercompany, accruals, prepayments, fixed assets and other financial statement line items as required by the Senior Financial Accountant and assisting with other month end and quarterly tasks including the preparation of disclosure packages and analytics.     Why join the team?   You’ll join a strong, values-driven finance team known for its collaboration, capability and supportive culture. This role offers exposure beyond core accounting, partnering with teams such as Business Intelligence and other finance teams while contributing to process improvements, automation and smarter ways of working.     D ay - to - day accountabilities :   Preparation of  timely  and  accurate  journal entries and reconciliations     Assistance  with preparation of supplementary monthly and quarterly close deliverables     Assistance  with periodic internal and external audit requirements      Assistance  with external financial reporting requirements including financial statements     Assistance  with ad hoc financial requests as  required     Identification and implementation of improvements relating to close process     Work closely with the FP&A team to analyse and understand actuals/inform the forecast      Adherence to internal control (SOX) requirements including maintenance of critical reports and spreadsheets       To read more about the role please click here to v iew j ob d escription     This is a Permanent position l ocated our Surry Hills, Sydney Campus .     Who you are   Minimum 3+ years’ relevant finance experience     Current CA or CPA designation is mandatory   Up to date and solid technical knowledge of IFRS accounting standards (US GAAP exposure is an advantage)    Advanced Excel    PeopleSoft (would be an advantage)   Experience operating within a well-established internal control environment in medium to large organisations.   Ability to work independently     Excellent communication, analytical, and organisational skills    Problem solving skills    High energy and proactive    Integrity/strong business ethics      Why join us?   Bold, modern and agile, we’re Australia’s fastest-growing university, going from 164 students in 2014 to 40,000+ alumni across 115+ countries and 2000+ staff today. In 2020, Australian Financial Review named us one of the country’s most innovative companies. As we continue to establish ourselves as a truly global university, we never lose sight of our student-centric approach. Supported by teams of passionate people, you’ll find endless opportunities for professional development and career progression.      We are proud to be an e qual opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, age, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation , disability , or any other protected characteristic.      We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people s for all positions.       Hiring process   We aim to provide you with the information you need at each stage of this process to help you present your best self. If you have any accessibility requirements, please contact your recruiter at maur.bell @torrens.edu.au for confidential support. We are committed to ensuring an equitable , barrier-free application process and have a Reasonable Adjustment Procedure in place to support you throughout the recruitment process.     To learn more about what makes Torrens University Australia a great place to work, visit https://www.torrens.edu.au/blog .     Applications close:    11th October - we will be reviewing applications as they are received.   Job r eference: R 31154 If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at yourcareer@torrens.edu.au"
    }
